# config.env of the K3 PD kit (2026-11-16): Kimi-K3 1P1D, P and D both TP8 + DCP8, KV over UALink (moriio FABRIC),
# on Helios trays of one vPOD. Every script sources it; the same file at the same path on every tray.
# ATOM_PD_COMMIT is the head of the PD tree that atom-k3pd-pd.bundle carries: the image's /app/ATOM plus this branch's
# three moriio commits. With the 1113 image that is this branch itself (746624d4 + b0fdb59d + 9eddd1ca + the recipe +
# the remote-lookup fix): git bundle create atom-k3pd-pd.bundle 746624d4..<branch>. With the 1116 image, cherry-pick the
# three onto its /app/ATOM (c7a0003c; they apply cleanly) and bundle c7a0003c..<that branch>.
IMAGE=rocm/fw-bringup:gfx1250-atom-k3-20261113
ATOM_PD_COMMIT=23cde1ae7ad1e0733b684f6b42f6c82703074474
KIT=/data/k3pd/kit           # this directory, on every tray (/kit in the containers)
WORK=/data/k3pd/work         # per serving tray: the container's /root/.cache (ATOM PD tree, launcher, logs, JIT caches)
MODEL_DIR=/data/k3           # Kimi-K3/ (f831ab66, /models/Kimi-K3) and Kimi-K3-DSpark/ (cf6b8244, /draft), every tray
CONTAINER=k3pd               # the server container of a serving tray
ROUTER_CONTAINER=k3pd_router # atomesh, on the router tray
NIC=enp4s0np0                # data-plane NIC: TP rendezvous, ZMQ side channel; KV goes over UALink, not this NIC
HANDSHAKE_PORT=6301          # moriio side channel base; rank r listens on base + r on its own tray

# An instance is two trays of one vPOD: TP ranks 0-3 on node0 (engine core, API :8000), 4-7 on node1. All four trays
# must be in the same vPOD (UALink carries the KV) and be power-cycled and loaded together (recover.sh, run from a fifth
# host). The names and addresses below are placeholders: put your trays (ssh names), their data-plane IPs and BMCs here.
P_NODE0=tray-a P_NODE0_IP=192.0.2.11
P_NODE1=tray-b P_NODE1_IP=192.0.2.12
D_NODE0=tray-c D_NODE0_IP=192.0.2.13
D_NODE1=tray-d D_NODE1_IP=192.0.2.14
ROUTER=tray-d ROUTER_IP=192.0.2.14 ROUTER_PORT=8100   # atomesh and the MLPerf client; no GPU work
BMC_USER=admin               # recover.sh: BMC login (password from ~/.k3pd_secret/askpass.sh), and the BMC host of
BMC_HOST_FMT=bmc-%s.example.com   # a tray (printf format, %s = the tray name)
P_SEQS=${P_SEQS:-64}         # max-num-seqs of P: it holds only what it prefills; each KDA slot costs KV pool (P6s)
D_SEQS=${D_SEQS:-512}        # max-num-seqs of D: the most that has run on 455 (1024 took the trays down). With
                             # DSpark k and ReplaySSM off, each request holds 1 + k KDA state slots (53.6 MiB a rank each)

CLIENT=/data/k3pd/client     # on the router tray: endpoints @ 4b385eb (endpoints/), the dataset (data/)
RESULTS=/data/k3pd/results   # on the router tray: one directory per run tag
